{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba .trellis/spec/backend/quality-guidelines.md | sed -n '1,65p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Quality Guidelines\n     2\t\n     3\t> Code quality standards for backend development.\n     4\t\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t## Overview\n     8\t\n     9\tBackend acceptance is fail-closed for evidence-to-report transformations. A green\n    10\tmodel constructor is not an integrity proof when later code can receive Pydantic\n    11\tinstances produced by `model_copy(update=...)`.\n    12\t\n    13\t---\n    14\t\n    15\t## Forbidden Patterns\n    16\t\n    17\t- Do not export a constructor/aggregator pair that accepts detached evaluated\n    18\t  results and stamps a new evidence snapshot or rule fingerprint onto them.\n    19\t- Do not trust `frozen=True` or construction-time validators at an authoritative\n    20\t  aggregation boundary; `model_copy(update=...)` does not re-run validation.\n    21\t- Do not accept report-gate results without independently deriving the complete\n    22\t  `(unit_id, object_id)` matrix from the current `GateSpec` and closed universe.\n    23\t\n    24\t---\n    25\t\n    26\t## Required Patterns\n    27\t\n    28\t- Public evaluation must be atomic: current rule + current closed snapshot +\n    29\t  current fact bindings go in; one immutable report result comes out.\n    30\t- Internal aggregate boundaries must re-derive content digests and identity keys\n    31\t  from the instance's current serialized content before semantic aggregation.\n    32\t- Rule content fingerprints, evidence snapshot identifiers, universe summaries,\n    33\t  and distinct immutable fact lineage must all participate in validation.\n    34\t\n    35\t---\n    36\t\n    37\t## Testing Requirements\n    38\t\n    39\t- Every authoritative Pydantic boundary needs a `model_copy` adversarial test.\n    40\t- Changed-snapshot and same-version changed-rule tests must prove recomputation,\n    41\t  not only key inequality.\n    42\t- Public-surface tests must verify unsupported detached constructors are absent,\n    43\t  while production call-site search verifies there is no alternate supported path.\n    44\t\n    45\t---\n    46\t\n    47\t## Code Review Checklist\n    48\t\n    49\t- Does any public path accept pre-evaluated unit results?\n    50\t- Does aggregation revalidate current content before reading semantic fields?\n    51\t- Are thresholds and the complete object matrix derived from the current spec?\n    52\t- Do parent results remain immutable during project-rule recomputation?\n    53\t- Do exact attacks, full regression, lint, strict typing, and package verification pass?\n    54\t\n    55\t## Scenario: Atomic evidence evaluation and batch-integrity revalidation\n    56\t\n    57\t### 1. Scope / Trigger\n    58\t\n    59\t- Trigger: adding or changing a gate evaluator, report result loader, evidence\n    60\t  snapshot, project-rule override, or any intermediate Pydantic batch used before\n    61\t  report acceptance.\n    62\t- Prevents: stale unit results being re-stamped under a new snapshot or changed\n    63\t  rule, and unvalidated `model_copy` mutations producing a false pass.\n    64\t\n    65\t### 2. Signatures\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
